<title>JAPAN: Japan PM wants strong yen, euro - Luxembourg PM.</title>
<headline>Japan PM wants strong yen, euro - Luxembourg PM.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto wants both the yen and the euro to be strong currencies, visiting Luxembourg Prime Minister Jean-Claude Juncker said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>In a meeting on Tuesday, Hashimoto told Juncker that Japan wanted the euro to be a strong currency, because that is what is needed in international transactions, Juncker said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Prime Minister Hashimoto indicated that he also wanted the yen to be a strong currency against the dollar and euro, because this was a prerequisite for the success of the reforms in Japan, mainly in the financial market,&quot; the statement said.  </p>
<p>The dollar earlier fell to about 122 yen on reports of the Hashimoto comment.</p>
<p>Luxembourg takes over the European Union presidency in July.</p>
</text>
